    "media:imagetext": "DO NOT OPERATE THE FOLLOWING WHILE ABOARD THE AIRCRAFT\nNO SMOKING\nEVACUATION ON WATER\nThere are eleven (11) 25-MAN LIFE RAFTS located in compartments\nwithin the aircraft cabin, marked:\n\"LIFE RAFT\"\nVisible Fluid Lighters\nElectric Computers\nFASTEN SEAT BELT\nIt is recommended that you\nkeep your Seat Belt\nLavatory\nEach 25-MAN LIFE RAFT weighs approximately\n130 Ibs. and should be removed by two able-bodied\npersons, carried to an EXIT, and secured to the aircraft\nprior to launching.\nfastened at all\ntimes while seated\nFasten\nBEFORE TAKEOFF AND LANDING\nSeat back up\nUnfasten\nBRACE POSITIONS\nEMERGENCY LANDING/DITCHING\nNine (9) LIFE RAFTS are\nstowed in the\noverhead (hatrack)\ncompartments.\nTwo (2) LIFE RAFTS\nare stowed in the\naft ceiling\ncompartments.\nTray table up\nCarry-on\nbaggage under\nseat\nAUTOMATIC OXYGEN SYSTEM\nNO SMOKING\nCAPACITY\nPERSONS\nLIFE RAFT INFLATION\n1. OXYGEN MASK LOCATION\nOxygen masks are stored in\na compartment above each\nrow of passenger seats.\nShould oxygen be required,\nthe compartment door\nwill open automatically\nand oxygen masks will\nbe presented on the door.\n2. USING THE MASK\nShould oxygen masks appear,\nremain seated. Grasp nearest\nmask and remove it from its\nholder, at the same time pulling free the cord connect.\ning mask to the compartment. This will permit the\noxygen to flow. Place mask over nose and mouth and\nbreathe normally. Continue to use oxygen until other-\nwise directed by a crew member.\n3. ADJUSTING THE\nMASK\nThe oxygen mask has an\nadjustable head strap to\nprovide a comfortable fit.\nIf mask is too tight, hold mask in position and pull\ngently on headband with free hand. If mask is too\nloose, pull tabs located where headband connects\nto oxygen mask.\nNORMAL CAPACITY\n25 PERSONS\nWARNING!\nDO NOT INFLATE LIFE RAFT INSIDE AIRCRAFT.\n1. Pull release latch\nmarked \"LIFE RAFT\"\ntowards aisle. Lift cover\naway from compartment\nand stow in overhead\nrack.\n1. Stand beside the\ncompartment and\npull release latch\nmarked \"LIFE RAFT\"\ntowards floor. Allow\ncompartment door\nto swing open\ntowards floor.\n2. Pull RED tab to\nrelease seat belt holding\nLIFE RAFT. Pull white\nstrap to roll raft out of\ncompartment. Grab assist\nstraps at fore and aft end\nof raft and lower to floor.\n2. Grab assist\nstraps at fore\nand aft end of raft\nand lower to floor.\nClose ceiling\ncompartment.\nA. Unsnap RED pouch marked \"LANYARD CORD\" and\nsecure spring snap at end of cord to seat leg, fastened\nseat belt or exposed door hinge nearest the exit.\nB. Position LIFE RAFT on exit threshold and\nunsnap HOT-PINK flap containing inflation\nhandle. Grasp this handle and pull hard as\nyou push LIFE RAFT out of aircraft.\nLIFE RAFT will inflate in approximately\n15 seconds.",
